1. The [Eb]Lord [Gm7]provides for [Gm]me [Cm]always,
For [Ab]each and [Eb]ev'ry care.
[Ab]And [G7]tho' the storms [Cm7]should [Ab]come,
I know [Eb]that Christ is always there.
[Bb]And who shall [Gm7]take salvation [G7]from [Cm]me,
[Bb7]Or [Ab]steal the grace [Bb]I've known?
[Ab]Not [G7]even [G]the [Cm]gates of [Ab]hell
Shall [Fm7]destroy the love that God has shown,
The love that God has [Bb]shown.

Chorus
[Cm]For I'm sure [Eb]that neither death, [Ab]nor life,
Nor height, nor [Eb]depth, [Cm7]nor [Fm]anything else [G]in the [Cm]world
Shall [Eb]be [Ab]able to [Cm7]cut us off from God,
[Cm]Shall be [Ab]able to [Cm]separate this Love,
[Gm7]In [Ab]Christ [Fm]Jesus, [F]we have won!
[Db]We have [C]won!

Verse 2
[Db]2. [F]Jesus [Am7]Christ is the [Dm]Answer,
[Cm7]I [Bb]need to [C7]search [C]no [F]more,
[Bb]For [Bbm]when [A]by grace [A7]He [Dm]called [D]to [Bb]me,
I [Dm]opened [D]wide the door.
[C]No [F]longer must [A]I [A7]fear the [Dm]Temptor,
[Cm7]Nor [Bb]face this [A7]life [Dm]alone:
[Bb]My [A7]Savior [A7]is [Dm]here to [Bb]stay,
Till [Dm]the day [Bbmaj7]He brings me home,
The [Gm7]day He brings [G7]me [C]home.
[A]Repeat [D]Chorus:
[Dm]For [F]I'm sure that neither [Bbmaj7]death, [Bb]nor life,
[C]Nor height, nor [F]depth, [D]nor anything [G]else [A]in the [Dm]world
[F]Shall [Am7]be [Bb]able to [Bbmaj7]cut [F]us off from [Fmaj7]God,
[D]Shall be [Bb]able to [D]separate [Dm]this [A]Love,
[Am]In [Dm7]Christ [Gm]Jesus, [G]we [Gm]have won!
